The newest bug on the bugpage at nethack.org lists this:

C342-55 fixed Dropping some of a set of cursed loadstones can 
              corrupt your inventory or crash the game.

This bug was first noticed (as far as I know) by 'madness'
on #nethack on irc.freenode.net, and another user, 'jilles'
first found out it was caused by dropping cursed luckstones.

Many people hammered at it, until these rules for replicating
the bug were found:

1. get 2 or more cursed loadstones in your inventory, in one stack.
2. move the item you want to duplicate into the next inventory slot.
   (eg, if loadstones are 'a', the next slot is 'b')
3. try to drop N loadstones. (where N is any number of loadstones
   in the stack, minus 1)
4. watch the dupe-stack grow by N, and look how you don't have N
   loadstones anymore.
5. If there is no item in the next inventory slot, nethack crashes.

It is possible that this bug was used during the tournament.

The bug is caused by a kludge that doesn't quite work as intended,
and is present in at least 3.4.2.

The kludge marks the loadstones to be dropped, and puts them into
the inventory chain after the loadstones not to be dropped.
(see invent.c)
Then, in do.c, the code tells the user that he cannot drop the
marked loadstones, and tries to put them back into the stack with
the other loadstones. Here is where the bug occurs:

                /* Kludge -- see invent.c */
                if (obj->corpsenm) {
                        struct obj *otmp;

                        otmp = obj;
                        obj = obj->nobj;
                        obj->quan += otmp->quan;
                        obj->owt = weight(obj);
                        freeinv(otmp);
                        obfree(otmp, obj);
                }

Note how this piece of code tries to put the marked loadstones back
into the _next_ object in the inventory chain, when the stack where
the other loadstones are is actually the _previous_ object in the chain.

Here is a diff that fixes the problem:  (not tested very thoroughly)
(This diff is also available from
http://cs.joensuu.fi/~pkalli/code/nh342-dupefix.diff)


--- nethack-3.4.2-orig/src/do.c	2003-08-30 03:07:28.000000000 +0300
+++ nethack-3.4.2-dupefix/src/do.c	2003-12-03 18:45:35.000000000 +0200
@@ -412,8 +412,9 @@
 		if (obj->corpsenm) {
 			struct obj *otmp;
 
-			otmp = obj;
-			obj = obj->nobj;
+			otmp = invent;
+			while (otmp && otmp->nobj && otmp->nobj != obj)
+			    otmp = otmp->nobj;
 			obj->quan += otmp->quan;
 			obj->owt = weight(obj);
 			freeinv(otmp);


